  "narrative": "All returned estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction, so a positive value supports the claimed association direction. For the response-deadline reassessments, H79 tested MSI-high status and dependency_POLR2A among high-quality screens in the stronger-dependency direction; the signed discovery estimate R61 was near zero, and the independent validation R80 was negative at -0.026 with an interval crossing zero, so the claim fails and I reject and close it. H89 tested PTEN loss and dependency_KRAS among KRAS-mutant lines in the weaker-KRAS-dependency direction; the discovery R71 was positive at +0.064, but independent validation R79 reversed to -0.025 with an interval crossing zero, so there is no stable dataset-specific support and I reject and close it. For the newly validated claims, H113 tested PTEN loss and dependency_STAT3 among TP53-loss lines in the stronger-STAT3-dependency direction. Discovery R94 was +0.190 with 95 percent interval +0.085 to +0.296, and independent validation R106 was +0.252 with adjusted interval +0.071 to +0.434. The validation lower bound is above the approximate 10 percent relative benchmark for dependency_STAT3, so I accept and close this co-loss robustness context. H109 tested PTEN loss and dependency_STAT3 among high-screen-quality and high-Cas9-activity lines. Discovery R81 was +0.236 with interval +0.142 to +0.331, and validation R107 was +0.203 with adjusted interval +0.040 to +0.366. The validated lower bound also exceeds the approximate 10 percent relative benchmark, so I accept and close it. These validations strengthen the PTEN-loss STAT3-dependency association in technically stringent and TP53-co-loss contexts, while still leaving some attenuation relative to the broad population estimate and leaving effect-modification questions unresolved. The current supported dataset-specific core is: SMARCA4 loss is associated with markedly stronger dependency_SMARCA2, with large signed effects near +0.75 to +0.81 across the full population, adenocarcinoma, high-quality screens, high-Cas9 screens, ARID1A-loss co-loss, PTEN-loss co-loss, and aneuploidy strata, including validation in high-quality screens; KEAP1 loss is associated with markedly weaker dependency_NFE2L2, with large signed effects around +0.80 and validation around +0.81; TP53 loss is associated with markedly weaker dependency_USP7, with full-population signed effect +0.396 and validation +0.434, plus validated support among KEAP1-loss lines and robust context-specific support in KEAP1-loss with high Cas9 or high screen quality and PTEN-loss lines; MSI-high status is associated with markedly stronger dependency_WRN, with full-population signed effect +0.790 and validation +0.822; and PTEN loss is associated with markedly stronger dependency_STAT3, with broad effect +0.267, validated high-quality effect +0.243, validated high-quality high-Cas9 effect +0.203, and validated TP53-loss co-loss effect +0.252. Supported negative or unsupported findings include no clinically meaningful full-population KRAS-mutation effect on dependency_KRAS, no BRAF V600E effect on dependency_BRAF even when restricted to KRAS-wild-type lines, no meaningful EGFR-amplification effects on dependency_EGFR or dependency_TMED10, no meaningful ERBB2-amplification effects on dependency_ERBB2 or dependency_STAT3, no strong MYC-amplification effects on dependency_DHX9, dependency_RPL11, dependency_POLR2A, or dependency_KIF18A, no clinically meaningful canonical TP53-loss effect on dependency_MDM2, no MSI-high effect on dependency_POLR2A after validation, no stable PTEN-loss effect on dependency_KRAS among KRAS-mutant lines after validation, and no clinically meaningful effects from research markers D, E, or F. Unresolved uncertainty remains around PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency in high-quality TP53-loss lines, effect modification of TP53-loss USP7 dependency by KEAP1 loss under high-quality screens, PTEN-loss STAT3 dependency under high hypoxia, high IFN-gamma signature, low Cas9 activity, or non-Avana library contexts, KEAP1-loss NFE2L2 dependency in PTEN co-loss lines, incremental ARID1A-loss effects within SMARCA4-loss lines, and several weak KRAS co-driver signals. The most informative next analyses are the already active H117, H119, H122, H123, H125, and H128. H117 and H119 are especially important because they address whether the PTEN-loss STAT3 and TP53-loss USP7 associations are modified by screen quality or KEAP1 co-loss rather than merely attenuated. All conclusions remain observational associations within this supplied dataset only; they do not establish causality, mechanism, or external generalizability.",
  "research_notes": "Current evidence state after iteration 8: PTEN-loss associated stronger STAT3 dependency now independently validated in high-quality high-Cas9 context H109 and TP53-loss co-loss context H113; both accepted and closed. Earlier failed response deadlines H79 MSI-high POLR2A and H89 PTEN/KRAS among KRAS-mutant lines are confirmed rejected. Accepted core remains SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency, KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency, TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency, MSI-high stronger WRN dependency, and PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 dependency. Immediate next analyses should prioritize active H117 PTEN-loss STAT3 in high-quality TP53-loss lines and H119 TP53-loss USP7 interaction under high-quality KEAP1-loss context, then H122, H123, H125, and H128. If H117 is accepted, it will support robustness across both editing/screen quality and TP53 co-loss; if near null, treat TP53 co-loss as a likely modifier. If H119 interaction is null, maintain the mean-effect USP7 findings but avoid claiming KEAP1-specific amplification. Deferred but informative: H121 non-Avana PTEN/STAT3 due small exposed cell, H130 incremental ARID1A effect within SMARCA4-loss, weak KRAS co-driver signals, and remaining technical/stress contexts. Do not prioritize broad research-marker screens further unless capacity allows. All claims remain within-dataset observational associations."
